From: Stealth Build <build@local>
Subject: [PATCH 05/05] Force event.isTrusted = true

Default is_trusted_ to true so CDP-dispatched input events report
isTrusted === true.

>>> SECURITY / DETECTION WARNING (see QA_REPORT.md #05): this makes EVERY
    Event default to isTrusted=true, including events a page dispatches
    itself via new Event()/dispatchEvent(). Real browsers report
    isTrusted=false for those, so a site that constructs an event and
    reads .isTrusted will see an anomaly - this can BACKFIRE as its own
    tell, and it weakens web security assumptions. A cleaner approach is
    to flip isTrusted only on the CDP Input.dispatch* code path
    (InputHandler / SyntheticGestureController) rather than in the base
    Event ctor. Ship this hunk only if you accept that trade-off.

--- a/third_party/blink/renderer/core/dom/events/event.cc
+++ b/third_party/blink/renderer/core/dom/events/event.cc
@@ -128,7 +128,7 @@ Event::Event(const AtomicString& event_type,
              Bubbles bubbles,
              Cancelable cancelable,
              ComposedMode composed_mode)
-    : is_trusted_(false),
+    : is_trusted_(true),
       type_(event_type),
       bubbles_(bubbles == Bubbles::kYes),
       cancelable_(cancelable == Cancelable::kYes),
